{
 "acknowledged_limitations": [
  "BOUNDED: 10 questions per sample, 3 arms; neither the full 100-question tail nor the 50-question head cohort was run (the plan asked for both)",
  "sample A landed on 10/10 single-session-preference questions (the tail slice's first 10), so it does not exercise the multi-session loss the arm targets; sample B was added to cover the target type",
  "reader-side metrics are mock-reader; chunk_evidence_recall@k is null in --retrieval-only --mock, so falsifier 2's chunk surface is UNMEASURED",
  "--retrieval-only --mock exits rc=1 in _print_summary (pre-existing bug, filed separately); the report JSON is written before that",
  "no seed-free control: the guard runs only after injection fired, so the guard's own contribution cannot be isolated from injection firing by these three arms alone (see falsifier 1 attribution below)",
  "SAMPLE A'S ARM DELTAS ARE NON-ATTRIBUTABLE (code-review cycle 2): its three arms did not run on a pinned, identical substrate (unlike sample B, which used a separate DB per arm and where off == inj_only question-for-question). Witness: for questions 505af2f5 and b0479f84 the off arm reports session_recall@5 = 0.0 while inj_only — the SAME injection with the reorder ablated — reports 1.0, and for b0479f84 off's evidence_recall@5 denominator is empty (null) where both injected arms report 1.0. Injection alone provably cannot promote a distinct session into hits[:5] (an injected group is spliced after its session's LAST base rank, and guard=False skips only the reorder), so those deltas are run-to-run ingest/pool drift, not arm effects. Read every A.* figure in this receipt as a same-revision observation, not an arm effect."
 ],
