  "2_surface_census": {
   "interpretation": "on the multi-session sample the marked evidence is not retrieved at k=5 by ANY arm (evidence_recall@5 == 0.0 for all 10 questions in all three arms): the reader-surface claim of part 2 of the confirmed problem is NOT supported here, and the arm neither raises it nor costs it. chunk_evidence_recall@k is unmeasurable under --retrieval-only --mock. Sample A's single-session questions DO have non-zero evidence recall and ON reports a common-denominator mean of 0.5 vs off's 0.4444 (+0.0556), with one previously vacuous question becoming evidence-bearing — but see the SAMPLE A non-attributability limitation: that sample's arms did not share a pinned substrate (off vs inj_only disagree where injection alone cannot move hits[:5]), so this A figure is NOT an arm effect. The reader-surface verdict rests on sample B alone, which is clean.",
